# Operator eng rails

Feature authors may have strong domain/IT context and **little software-engineering
judgment**. Cursor must not invent client-side eng invariants.

## Always owned by engineering rails (do not freestyle)

- Director capability gates (not “any logged-in TD”)  
- No client engines duplicating backend generate/score/standings  
- No dual SSOT clients (`calculate*` / `process*` beside live GETs)  
- Identity keys = `user_id` for logic  
- Render safety (effects/deps — no update-depth loops)  
- API error envelope / timeout handling conventions  
- Cross-repo contract sync same delivery window  

If a prompt would violate these, **refuse the unsafe shape**, propose the safe
shape, and cite the rule (`no-client-engines.mdc`, `react-render-safety.mdc`).

## When implementing operator prompts

1. Prefer `src/features/*`, shared form sections, report registry  
2. Phased plan before coding (`agent-commit-partition.mdc`)  
3. List eng risks for the steward timezone  
4. Add tests for the unsafe UI case (locked controls, wrong pool selected)

## Do not tell the operator

- “Be careful about React hooks” without a concrete fix  
- Dual clients OK as polish  
- Large unrelated refactors mixed into the feature ship
